 3. 💰 Golden age for big biz 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: U.S. Bureau of Economic Analysis, FactSet. Chart: Axios/Matt Phillips Corporate America is raking in record profits, luxuriating in luscious margins and capturing the largest chunk of the country's income on record, Axios Markets co-author Matt Phillips writes. 

 Why it matters: The corporate bonanza is bolstering the stock market, but it may also be fueling Americans' sour mood. Today is the unofficial start of third-quarter earnings season. Wall Street expects S&amp;P 500 members will continue to make it rain. 

 👓 Between the lines: The market is still all about AI, but the gains are extremely concentrated.

 Ben Snider, chief U.S. equity analyst with Goldman Sachs, notes more than two-thirds of total growth in S&amp;P 500 earnings is expected to come from just 10 stocks. Keep reading . 

 
 
