 4. 🌾 Scoop: Kansas rescue mission 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Sen. Roger Marshall (R-Kansas) holds a "jaws of life" rescue device while visiting the Topeka Fire Department on Thursday. Photo: Evert Nelson/The Topeka Capital-Journal via Reuters A top Trump political operative has been tapped to help boost Kansas Sen. Roger Marshall's campaign in the weeks before the Nov. 3 election — the latest sign of how Republicans are scrambling to defend the red-state seat, Axios' Alex Isenstadt writes. 

 The hiring of veteran strategist Chris Grant reflects the GOP's growing anxiety over Kansas' Senate race. Marshall is running neck and neck with Democrat Adam Hamilton in a state President Trump won by 16 points in 2024. Why it matters: Republicans fear losing Kansas could be a domino in costing them their Senate majority.

 🔎 Zoom in: GOP operatives have become increasingly frustrated with Marshall's reelection campaign, which they believe hasn't been aggressive enough at a time when soaring fuel prices have particularly hurt farmers in Kansas and elsewhere in the Midwest.

 Grant, who helped lead the main pro-Trump super PAC in 2024 and has remained involved in Trump's political operation, will be a senior adviser to Marshall and help guide strategy in the final three weeks. Keep reading . 

 
 
