 7. 🚨 Scary supermarket hack 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Illustration: Sarah Grillo/Axios

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Hackers raised the temperature of refrigerators and freezers at hundreds of French supermarkets to as high as 122°F yesterday, causing fires and spoiling food.

 Stores in Spain, Portugal, Poland, Germany and Belgium were also affected. The attacks resemble disruptions reported at about a dozen U.S. military commissaries in late August that led to food losses after fridges were affected.

