 8. 🪓 &quot;Tim-ber!&quot; is the new &quot;Fore!&quot; 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 A golfer hits a ball from the fairway near log sections cut from trees at the East Potomac Golf Links in D.C. yesterday. Photo: Mark Schiefelbein/AP A "furious" district court judge ordered a 24-hour halt to a massive tree-cutting operation at the historic East Potomac Golf Course in D.C. that President Trump plans to overhaul.

 Government lawyers said at a holiday emergency hearing that about 430 trees were cut down on Saturday. 299 more are slated for removal. The scene at East Potomac Golf Links yesterday. Photo: Mark Schiefelbein/AP Kevin Griess, the superintendent of the National Mall and Memorial Parks, cited a 2019 National Park Service Cultural Landscape Report as the guide for the work, which he said was part of Trump's 2025 order to make D.C. safe and beautiful.

